{"kind":"propose","text":"The H2 proof inventory has two undetermined rows. Section 5.2 names the allocation fact in position and the resolution or expiry fact in terminal input. Sections 5.2 and 5.5 name `uses` for the observed order head and member cut entries but do not say whether position and terminal references also retain foreign proof bytes. I propose that the references alone charge only their sealed entry bytes, and that any actual retained order copy is charged separately as an entry plus possible birth, deduplicated across retained keys. The prepare always quotes 2E for the observed order head and for each declared cut proof not already covered by that head, plus its declared page bound. If H4 or H6 needs the allocation, resolution or expiry bytes retained locally, please name those exact uses now so H2 can charge them. The current selected-form quote includes the prepare and terminal entry allowances and leaves a complete attempt unavailable until this proof inventory is known. H3 still supplies the validated order definition for the order-side allocation/outcome quote."}